# i18n coverage exemptions — consumed by scripts/i18n-coverage-check.sh.
# Every language-bearing distribution file that is NOT managed under i18n/ja/ must be listed
# here with an explicit reason category; anything unlisted fails CI. Format (one per line):
#   <category> <glob-relative-to-plugin-root>     (POSIX `case` glob; `*` crosses `/`)
# Categories:
#   lang-specific   — JA-only by nature; deployment is language-gated at setup time, never translated
#   output-template — skeleton for user artifacts; document language is chosen at generation time
#                     (orthogonal to the harness language)
#   dev-doc         — maintainer-facing documentation; JA trigger exemplars are legitimate content
#   active-only     — deliberately bilingual / runtime files kept out of the i18n trees
#                     (set-language invariant: the switcher must survive materialization)
#   neutral         — no natural-language prose worth localizing (schemas, samples)
lang-specific   templates/rules/writing-ja.md
lang-specific   templates/ja-style-core.md
output-template templates/specs/*
output-template templates/ci/*
dev-doc         templates/README.md
dev-doc         templates/docs/_common-pattern.md
active-only     skills/set-language/*
neutral         templates/odd/*
